{
  "schema": "airlock.tamper_matrix.v0",
  "about": "Expected result per cell of the tamper matrix. tests/e2e_tamper_matrix.sh (jq) and tests/tamper_matrix.rs (serde_json) both read this file and apply the same ops. A cell is `assemble` then `verify --no-sign --no-witness --require-claim <require_claim>` on the (possibly tampered) request. `findings` is the sorted unique set of artifact_class, with detector hits written as DETECTED_SENSITIVE:<rule_id>. ANNOTATED cells carry derived_text_field_hit because the annotated fixture assembles derived text and the scanner records a finding for every derived-text leaf. Payloads are fabricated; the AWS-shaped token is random, not a credential.",
  "model": "gpt-5",
  "require_claim": "RAW_DOCUMENT_ABSENT",
  "modes": ["ANNOTATED", "TELEMETRY_ONLY"],
  "policy": "fixtures/tamper_matrix/policy.yaml",
  "input": "fixtures/annotated_mode/strategy_space.json",
  "system_prompt": "fixtures/annotated_mode/system_prompt.txt",
  "leak_pointer": "/heuristic_reference/bundle_id",
  "chain": {
    "about": "Constants for the chain_turn site. A chain_turn cell is `assemble --prior-receipt R --response RESPONSE --response-adapter ADAPTER --prior-manifest PRIOR_MANIFEST [--tool-result TOOL_USE_ID=ARTIFACT]` then the same verify as every other cell. R is built by the harness in the shape `airlock gate` writes (the gate's receipt is unsigned, and this one is hand-built, not written by a gate). Every response and artifact is a committed file, so jq and serde_json hand the binary identical bytes; each hash below is of the exact file bytes, and the binary re-checks it on every run (assemble refuses when a response does not match its receipt or the receipt does not name the prior manifest), so a wrong constant fails the cell and never passes quietly.",
    "adapter": "anthropic_messages",
    "prior_manifest": "fixtures/clean_telemetry_only/expected_manifest.json",
    "prior_manifest_hash": "blake3:d374b9c7b8c9e0eba9b1cae5fc8835d3bc43d86b28bc8fe4646ec4adddd70f04",
    "tool_use_id": "toolu_fx_0001",
    "responses": {
